# The earlier releases gh-touchid knows, by the cdhash of each architecture of their signed bin/gh-touchid.
# scripts/build.sh --known-releases builds this list into a release (knownReleaseList in BuildConfiguration.swift).
# A release trusts the background program and the clients of a release listed `trusted` as it trusts its own. One
# listed `revoked` it no longer trusts: it locks that release's background program, and the sessions held there end,
# nothing carried over (each program runs `gh-touchid session` again). The release workflow appends each release it
# publishes, with the cdhashes read from the signed binary (`codesign -d -vvv --arch ARCH`); marking a release
# revoked is a change made by hand.
#
# One release per line, `VERSION STATUS arm64=CDHASH x86_64=CDHASH`: STATUS is trusted or revoked, each CDHASH is 40
# lowercase hex digits. Lines starting with # and empty lines are ignored.
